artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider type IIB superstring theory on the background AdS_3 × S^3 × M^4 (where M^4 is either T^4 or K3), supported by NS-NS and/or R-R three-form flux, with AdS_3 of radius set by the level k of the underlying current algebra. The AdS/CFT correspondence asserts that this string theory is dual to a two-dimensional boundary conformal field theory (e.g. a deformation of the symmetric orbifold Sym^N(M^4)).

Provide an exact, nonperturbative formulation of this worldsheet string theory on AdS_3 × S^3 × M^4 — including a complete description of its physical spectrum, vertex operators, and Hilbert space (with all spectrally flowed sectors of the underlying SL(2,R) WZW model) — and use this formulation to:

(a) compute n-point correlation functions of physical string states in the bulk AdS_3 worldsheet theory, for arbitrary n and arbitrary values of the level k and the flux moduli;

(b) match these worldsheet correlators with the corresponding correlation functions of the dual boundary two-dimensional conformal field theory, thereby establishing a rigorous, correlator-level check of the AdS_3/CFT_2 correspondence;

(c) reconstruct the boundary conformal field theory (its operator content, OPEs and moduli space) directly from the exact worldsheet data.

The problem is to carry out (a), (b), and (c) for general k (in particular away from the minimal-tension point k = 1) and for general background fluxes interpolating between the pure NS-NS and pure R-R points.

